    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Stan users,<div><br></div><div>I have trying to use rstanarm as a template for writing a new R package &quot;eggCounts&quot;, I followed the list in </div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/35905529/using-rstanrstan-package-skeleton-to-add-to-existing-r-package\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/35905529/using-rstanrstan-package-skeleton-to-add-to-existing-r-package&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461785310000&amp;usg=AOvVaw19dMXEpO-vTPJ0q_1zOJaN\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/35905529/using-rstanrstan-package-skeleton-to-add-to-existing-r-package</a></div><div><br></div><div>, except that my inst/chunks subdirectory is an empty folder, and I also copied the .onLoad part of zzz.R. I have encountered the following errors/questions so far..:</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>1. if I add useDynLib(eggCounts, .registration = TRUE), it gives me <br></div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;width:588px;padding:6px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;!important;font-size:10.4pt!important;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">Error in library.dynam(lib, package, package.lib) : \r\n  shared object ‘eggCounts.so’ not found</pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;width:588px;padding:6px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">Is this because I didn&#39;t install eggCounts in the first place? I thought this is to prepare the </span><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">RcppModules, without the useDynLib() I have the error</span></font></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;width:588px;padding:6px\"><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;width:588px;padding:6px;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important\"><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;!important;font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important;outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;width:588px;padding:6px;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important\">Error : .onLoad failed in loadNamespace() for &#39;eggCounts&#39;, details:\r\n  call: value[[3L]](cond)\r\n  error: failed to load module stan_fit4paired_mod from package eggCounts\r\nFailed to initialize module pointer: Error in FUN(X[[i]], ...): no such symbol _rcpp_module_boot_stan_fit4paired_mod in package eggCounts</pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;!important;font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important;outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;width:588px;padding:6px;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important\"><span style=\"font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;line-height:inherit;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13.8667px\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><br></font></span></pre><pre style=\"text-align:left;color:rgb(0,0,0);outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;width:588px;padding:6px;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;!important;font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important\"><span style=\"font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;line-height:inherit;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13.8667px\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Ubuntu Mono\">2</font></span><span style=\"font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;line-height:inherit;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-size:13px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;white-space:normal\">. I also had this error, I am using Linux server at my university</span><br></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;width:588px;padding:6px;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;line-height:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Warning: file &#39;eggCounts/cleanup&#39; did not have execute permissions: corrected</span></pre></pre></pre></div><div><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;width:588px;padding:6px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;!important;font-size:10.4pt!important;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;width:588px;padding:6px;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;!important;font-size:10.4pt!important;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;white-space:normal;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;line-height:inherit\">3. In Rstudio if I click Load All, it creates several files in src/ then everything seems to work fine after Build and Reload the package again.</span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;width:588px;padding:6px;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;!important;font-size:10.4pt!important;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;white-space:normal;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;line-height:inherit\"><br></span></pre></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;width:588px;padding:6px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;!important;font-size:10.4pt!important;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;white-space:normal\">Thanks for any suggestions,</span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;width:588px;padding:6px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;!important;font-size:10.4pt!important;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;white-space:normal\">Craig</span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;width:588px;padding:6px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;!important;font-size:10.4pt!important;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-heigh